l, God. The MANY side model would be Human. Each God could have MANY Humans following him/her through a JOIN model of GuardianAngel. The God model could have many GuardianAngels but lets say s/he doesn\u2019t care about keeping track of all his/her follower Humans. Who said DB associations were boring?","topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"jswanner/arel-haversine","owner":"jswanner","html_url":"https://github.com/jswanner/arel-haversine","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"Provides haversine formula, implemented with Arel.","topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"sfaxon/ws-github-webhook","owner":"sfaxon","html_url":"https://github.com/sfaxon/ws-github-webhook","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"bambery/cloud_crooner","owner":"bambery","html_url":"https://github.com/bambery/cloud_crooner","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"Manage your Sinatra app's assets with Sprockets and sync them to Amazon S3","topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"michaelfairley/pinguin","owner":"michaelfairley","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelfairley/pinguin","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"weiser/the-presidents","owner":"weiser","html_url":"https://github.com/weiser/the-presidents","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"emmath/q_plus_a","owner":"emmath","html_url":"https://github.com/emmath/q_plus_a","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"emmath/important_dates","owner":"emmath","html_url":"https://github.com/emmath/important_dates","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1769},{"name":"koos42/domain_categorization","owner":"koos42","html_url":"https://github.com/koos42/domain_categorization","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language